ests see on the website are maintained in the website content. Editing the list here would not change the enquiry form, so those controls are hidden.</p><div class="single-admin"><strong>Keep the choices in sync</strong><p>Ask the website manager to update the guest form when an event option needs to be added or renamed.</p></div></section><?php elseif($tab==='payments'):?><form class="settings-card-form narrow" method="post"><h2>Payment Settings</h2><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<?=sh($_SESSION['csrf'])?>"><p class="helper-text">Set how many payments can be recorded for one confirmed booking.</p><label>Maximum payments per booking<select name="max_payment_steps"><?php for($i=1;$i<=5;$i++):?><option <?=$i==(int)($s['max_payment_steps']??5)?'selected':''?>><?=$i?></option><?php endfor;?></select></label><fieldset><legend>Payment Methods</legend><p class="helper-text">Only checked methods will appear when recording a payment.</p><?php foreach(['cash'=>'Cash','bank-transfer'=>'Bank Transfer','upi'=>'UPI','cheque'=>'Cheque','card'=>'Card','other'=>'Other'] as $value=>$label):?><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" name="payment_methods[]" value="<?=sh($value)?>" <?=in_array($value,$methods,true)?'checked':''?>><span><?=sh($label)?></span></label><?php endforeach;?></fieldset><div class="single-admin"><strong>Tell the guest about the payment plan</strong><p>Payment terms are not sent automatically. Explain the agreed schedule to the guest before recording payments.</p></div><button class="primary-button" name="action" value="save_payments">Save Payment Settings</button></form>
<?php elseif($tab==='rules'):?><section class="settings-card-form narrow"><h2>Statuses &amp; reminders</h2><p class="helper-text">Enquiry and booking statuses are built into the admin workflow and cannot be switched off here. Change an individual record from its details screen.</p><div class="single-admin"><strong>Reminders are manual</strong><p>Setting a reminder adds it to the record. The panel does not send automatic reminder messages.</p></div></section><?php elseif($tab==='email'):?><?php $resendKeySaved=booking_resend_key($db,$config)!=='';?><section class="settings-card-form narrow email-setup-card"><div class="settings-heading"><div><h2>Email setup</h2><p>Connect Resend to send venue emails.</p></div><span class="email-status <?= $resendKeySaved?'saved':'pending' ?>"><?= $resendKeySaved?'Key saved · not tested':'Setup needed' ?></span></div><div class="single-admin email-provider-note"><strong>Before you connect</strong><p>Verify your sending domain in Resend and add the DNS records it provides. Then create a sending-only API key restricted to that domain and paste it below. After saving the key, Resend will deliver new-enquiry alerts and manual email actions. Until then, the existing website mail method remains active.</p></div><form method="post"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<?=sh($_SESSION['csrf'])?>"><div class="form-grid email-fields"><label>Resend API key<input type="password" name="resend_api_key" autocomplete="new-password" spellcheck="false" placeholder="<?= $resendKeySaved?'Saved securely — enter a new key only to replace it':'Paste your re_ API key when ready' ?>"><small>Encrypted before storage; the saved key is never shown. Leave blank to keep it.</small></label><label>Sender name<input name="email_sender_name" maxlength="120" required value="<?=sh($s['email_sender_name']??($config['email_from_name']??'Late Venutai Chavan Multipurpose Hall'))?>"><small>Shown in the guest’s inbox.</small></label><label>Verified sender email<input type=